    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d612">

                <pb facs="0636" n="520" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg520"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/1308.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Chargé Davis</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-09-15T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 15, 1915, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your September 15, 10 a.m. It would seem desirable that Haitian Government make
                    reply to the effect that legitimate German interests will be accorded the same
                    equitable and impartial treatment as will be given to all foreigners and foreign
                    interests in Haiti.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
